lchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{U}","name":"Turn to Frog","oracle_id":"74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67","oracle_text":"Until end of turn, target creature loses all abilities and becomes a blue Frog with base power and toughness 1/1.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2024-02-23","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Wake Thrasher","oracle_id":"f2d1e991-e13a-43c7-85aa-d53dd14822e6","oracle_text":"Whenever a permanent you control becomes untapped, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2017-10-24","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Merfolk Soldier"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Effects that modify a creature’s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Titanic Growth, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness.","oracle_id":"74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If one of the Theros block Gods is affected by Turn to Frog, it will be a legendary 1/1 blue Frog enchantment creature with no abilities. If it stops being a creature, perhaps because your devotion to its color(s) decreased, it will be a legendary blue enchantment with no abilities. The way continuous effects work, the God’s type-changing ability is applied before the effect that removes that ability is applied.","oracle_id":"74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the affected creature gains an ability after Turn to Frog resolves, it will keep that ability.","oracle_id":"74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The creature will lose all other colors and creature types, but it will retain any other card types (such as artifact) or supertypes (such as legendary) it may have.","oracle_id":"74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Turn to Frog doesn’t counter abilities that have already triggered or been activated. In particular, there is no way to cast this spell to stop a creature’s ability that says “At the beginning of your upkeep,” “When this creature enters the battlefield,” or similar from triggering.","oracle_id":"74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Turn to Frog overwrites all previous effects that set the creature’s base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply after Turn to Frog resolves will overwrite this effect.","oracle_id":"74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Rally of Wings affects only creatures you control at the time it resolves. Creatures that gain flying later in the turn or that you begin to control later in the turn won't get +2/+2.","oracle_id":"984336a7-85bd-4549-9771-03a0c2367db0","published_at":"2019-05-03","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If permanents you control become untapped during your untap step, Wake Thresher’s ability will trigger that many times. However, since no player gets priority during the untap step, those abilities wait to be put on the stack until your upkeep starts. At that time, all your “beginning of upkeep” triggers will also trigger. You can put them and Wake Thresher’s abilities on the stack in any order.","oracle_id":"f2d1e991-e13a-43c7-85aa-d53dd14822e6","published_at":"2008-08-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To work as an evasion ability, an attacking creature must already have flying when the declare blockers step begins. Once a creature has become blocked, giving it flying won’t change that.","oracle_id":"f7518456-45ed-41d4-bd3c-5aacea28eb35","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
